According to 3GPP TS 38.331, upon reception of RRCReject, the UE is required to:

"Abort the current establishment or resumption procedure and inform the upper layers about the RRC connection establishment or resumption failure."

Additionally, the UE shall:

* Release the RRC connection;
* Perform a release of the signalling connection to the upper layers;
* Enter RRC_IDLE state.

Exact statement from spec: 
"Upon receiving the RRCReject, the UE shall:
[...]
- Abort the current establishment or resumption procedure;
- Release the RRC connection;
- Perform a release of the signalling connection to the upper layers;
- Enter RRC_IDLE state."

According to 3GPP TS 38.331, for NR sidelink groupcast or broadcast communication, the UE reports its interested services with sidelink DRX by including the "SidelinkInterestInfo" in the UEAssistanceInformation message. Specifically, it reports the "SL-DRX-Info" which includes the sidelink DRX configuration for the interested services.

More precisely, as per TS 38.331, section 6.2.2:

"The UE may report sidelink DRX information for sidelink groupcast or broadcast communication by including SidelinkInterestInfo in UEAssistanceInformation."

And, 

"SidelinkInterestInfo ::= SEQUENCE { 
    ...
    sl-DRX-Info  SL-DRX-Info OPTIONAL,
    ... 
}"

and 

"SL-DRX-Info ::= SEQUENCE {
    drx-Cycle  ENUMERATED { 
        drx-cycle-128ms, 
        drx-cycle-256ms, 
        drx-cycle-512ms, 
        drx-cycle-1024ms 
    },
    ...
}"

According to 3GPP TS 38.331, the UE tries to establish or resume an RRC connection when it is in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE state and it has a pending uplink transmission, or when it receives a paging message, or when it has a request to perform an MO (Mobile Originated) call or SMS, or when it has a request to perform a MO data transmission. 

More specifically, as stated in TS 38.331, 5.3.1: 
"The UE shall try to establish or resume an RRC connection, e.g. for:
- Paging (see clause 5.4);
- Initial UE message (e.g. for MO-SMS or MO-data);
- A request to perform a MO call or MO-SMS;
- A request to perform a MO data transmission;
- UE triggered update (e.g. for periodic registration, for a change of UE capability, or for a PLMN change)."
